# Overview

The software is a console-based Hangman game written in C++. The player is presented with a randomly selected word (from a built-in word list) as a series of blanks, and must guess it one letter at a time. Wrong guesses are tracked visually through an ASCII-art gallows that progressively "builds" toward a loss. The game includes a hint system that lets the player reveal a hidden letter at the cost of a wrong guess, adding a strategic trade-off. The game loops until the player wins, loses, or chooses to stop replaying.

[Software Demo Video](https://youtu.be/h5ZvPcEjZSk)

